-- title:
--   Hecke set at a good prime is a single double coset
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b$ be rational numbers and $q'$ a prime, and suppose [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q'`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_EichlerOrder.html#L87) holds, i.e. $a<0$, $b<0$ and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ the algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra (every non-zero element a unit) precisely when $q'$ lies in $v$. Let $R$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ which is an Eichler order of level $N$, that is, $R=\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ for two orders $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2$ each maximal among orders under inclusion, with the relative index of $R$ in $\Lambda_1$ (as additive subgroups) equal to $N$. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\nmid N$ and $\ell\neq q'$. Write $\widehat R$ for [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox R`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14), the additive subgroup of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{\mathrm f}$ generated by the tensors $z\otimes \alpha$ with $z\in R$ and $\alpha$ a finite adele integral at every place, and $U=$ [`Submodule.finiteIdeleStabilizer R`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L26) for the stabiliser of $\widehat R$, viewed as a set, in the unit group of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{\mathrm f}$. The Hecke set [`QuaternionAlgebra.primeHeckeSet R ℓ`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_ClassSetHecke.html#L109) consists of those units $h$ with $h\in\widehat R$, $\ell\, h^{-1}\in\widehat R$, $h^{-1}\notin\widehat R$ and $\ell^{-1}h\notin\widehat R$. The assertion is that if $g$ belongs to this Hecke set, then the Hecke set equals the double coset $UgU$.
--
--   This is the classical statement that, at a prime $\ell$ not dividing the level and distinct from the ramified prime, the local Hecke correspondence of an Eichler order is given by a single double coset of the idelic unit group $\widehat R^{\times}$, so that the four integrality conditions defining the Hecke set can be replaced by membership in $\widehat R^{\times} g\,\widehat R^{\times}$ for any one Hecke idele $g$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, both for the index computation of the stabiliser of an intersected order and for producing the degeneracy data of the level-$\ell$ storey of the class-set tower.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_primeHeckeSet_eq_doubleCoset_finiteIdeleStabilizer.lean

